task: find quickest schedule

problem descr: using drones to deliver customer orders from warehouses in a 2D grid
- drones: max weight, start at warehouse 0
- warehouse: location, inventory of products
- customer order: location, list of products
--> goal: schedule drone actions to minimize time to deliver all orders



entities:
- map + coordinates: 2D grid /w euclidean distance

- products: 
  - multiple product types, 
  - a product type has a fixed weight

- warehouses:
  - location (x,y)
  - inventory of products (by type and quantity)
    - eg: [5, 1, 0, 3] means 5 of product type 0, 1 of type 1, none of type 2, 3 of type 3

- orders:
  - delivery location (x,y)
  - list of items (by type and quantity)
    - eg: [0, 2, 1, 0] means 2  items of type 1, 1 of type 2, none of type 0 or 3

- drones:
  - id: 
    (start)-location: (0, 0)
    max_weight: 
  - commands:
    - load     d+1 turns
    - deliver  d+1 turns
    - wait     w turns
    - unload   d+1 turns
  - travel time: ceil(euclidean distance) rounded up to next int 
  - action time: 1 turn per load, deliver or unload action
    - eg: distance 2.3 & load --> travel time 3 turns + 1 turn to load = 4 turns total

- simulation:
  - runs for T turns (0 to T-1)
  - drones execute commands chronologically
  - case: multiple commands in same warehouse --> unload before load
  - orders earn points based on how quickly they are fulfilled
    - points =  (T - turn order completed) / T * 100 


file format: 
  1st section: simulation parameters
  - no of rows in grid
  - no of columns in grid
  - no of drones
  - no of turns 
  - max weight a drone can carry
  2nd section: product availability
  - no of product types
  - weights of each product type
  3rd section: warehouse info
  - no of warehouses
  - for each warehouse:
    - location (row, col)
    - inventory of products (by type and quantity)
  4th section: customer orders
  - no of orders
  - for each order:
    - delivery location (row, col)
    - no of items
    - list of items (by type and quantity)



--> output file:
- integer Q: no of commands
  - for each command:
    - drone id
    - command type (L, D, W, U)
    - parameters (warehouse id, order id, product type id, quantity)

# notes
  # - load: L --> params: warehouse id, product type id, quantity
  # - deliver: D --> params: customer id, product type id, quantity
  # - wait: W --> params: wait time
  # - unload: U --> params: warehouse id, product type id, quantity

  # fly to warehouse/customer location and deliver/load/unload x items of product type y





